{% extends "tool_layout" %}
{% import "icons" as icons %}

{# js/tools/pages/jwt-decoder.mjs #}

{% block tool %}
<section class="panel panel-pad tool-panel" aria-labelledby="jwt-heading">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center gap-3">
        <div>
            <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-1" id="jwt-heading">Token</h2>
            <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">Paste a JWT. A <code>Bearer</code> prefix and line breaks are fine.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" id="jwt-clear">{{ icons.icon("eraser") }} Clear</button>
    </div>
    <label for="jwt-in" class="visually-hidden">JSON Web Token</label>
    <textarea id="jwt-in" class="form-control tool-area mt-3 jwt-in" rows="4" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
        placeholder="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIn0.signature"
        aria-describedby="jwt-error"></textarea>
    <div id="jwt-error" class="small text-warn mt-1" role="status"></div>
    <div id="jwt-summary" class="chips mt-2" role="status"></div>
</section>

<div id="jwt-decoded" hidden>
    <div class="row g-3 mt-0">
        <div class="col-lg-5">
            <section class="panel panel-pad" aria-labelledby="jwt-header-heading">
                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-0" id="jwt-header-heading">Header</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" data-copy="jwt-header" aria-label="Copy header">{{ icons.icon("copy") }}</button>
                </div>
                <textarea id="jwt-header" class="form-control tool-area jwt-json mt-2" rows="4" readonly aria-label="Header JSON"></textarea>
            </section>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-7">
            <section class="panel panel-pad" aria-labelledby="jwt-payload-heading">
                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-0" id="jwt-payload-heading">Payload (claims)</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" data-copy="jwt-payload" aria-label="Copy payload">{{ icons.icon("copy") }}</button>
                </div>
                <textarea id="jwt-payload" class="form-control tool-area jwt-json mt-2" rows="4" readonly aria-label="Payload JSON"></textarea>
                <dl id="jwt-claims" class="jwt-claims mt-3 mb-0"></dl>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="panel panel-pad tool-panel mt-3" aria-labelledby="jwt-verify-heading">
        <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-1" id="jwt-verify-heading">Check the signature</h2>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3" id="jwt-key-help"></p>
        <div id="jwt-secret-box">
            <label for="jwt-secret" class="visually-hidden">Secret</label>
            <input id="jwt-secret" class="form-control font-monospace" type="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="The shared secret" data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true" data-bwignore="true" data-form-type="other">
            <div class="form-check mt-2">
                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="jwt-secret-b64">
                <label class="form-check-label small" for="jwt-secret-b64">The secret is base64-encoded</label>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="jwt-public-box">
            <label for="jwt-public" class="visually-hidden">Public key</label>
            <textarea id="jwt-public" class="form-control tool-area" rows="5" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----&#10;...&#10;-----END PUBLIC KEY-----&#10;&#10;or a JWK, or a JWKS ({&quot;keys&quot;: [...]})"></textarea>
        </div>
        <p id="jwt-verify-result" class="jwt-verify mt-3 mb-0" role="status"></p>
    </section>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block about %}
<h2 class="h4">What is a JWT?</h2>
<p>A JSON Web Token (JWT, said "jot") is a small, signed message that says who someone is and what they're
    allowed to do, used for logins and API access. It's three parts separated by dots: a <strong>header</strong>
    saying how it's signed, a <strong>payload</strong> of claims, and a <strong>signature</strong>. The header and
    payload are only base64url-encoded, not encrypted: anyone who has the token can read them, which is all this
    decoder does.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Is it safe to paste a token here?</h2>
<p>A token is often a live login: whoever has it can act as you until it expires. This page decodes and checks
    it entirely in your browser, and never sends it anywhere, but be careful with any site that does. When
    you're done, tokens you've shared can usually be revoked by logging out.</p>

<h2 class="h4">The standard claims</h2>
<p><code>iss</code> is who issued the token, <code>sub</code> who it's about, and <code>aud</code> who it's for.
    <code>exp</code>, <code>nbf</code> and <code>iat</code> are when it expires, when it starts being valid and
    when it was issued, as Unix timestamps; this page shows them as dates. <code>jti</code> is a unique ID for the
    token.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Checking the signature</h2>
<p>A signature proves the token wasn't changed since it was signed. Tokens signed with <code>HS256</code>,
    <code>HS384</code> or <code>HS512</code> use a shared secret: enter it to check. The others (<code>RS</code>,
    <code>PS</code>, <code>ES</code> and <code>EdDSA</code>) are checked with the issuer's public key, as a PEM
    block or a JWK. Many issuers publish theirs as a JWKS at an address ending in
    <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code>; paste the whole set and the key the token names is used. A token with
    <code>"alg": "none"</code> isn't signed at all.</p>
{% endblock %}
